  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper presents an end-to-end gate-based QAOA for the discrete global minimum variance portfolio problem using binary block encoding, a hard qubit-excitation mixer, and classical optimizers DA and COBYLA. It studies small instances with n = 4 to 6 assets and l = 2 to 5 binary block lengths, using Nm = 16 optimization shots and NM = 65536 post-optimization shots, and concludes that thermal-relaxation noise prevents practical quantum advantage despite some favorable scaling trends in sampling probability.",
  "experiments": [
